RetroBoot: allow slow ARM hosts enough translation time during Quadra calibration.

The existing VIA timer-2 hold protects the ROM's delay-loop calibration from
TCG translation pauses, but its 4 ms maximum can expire in the middle of the
first-time instruction window. The earlier injected 14-block/4.2 ms test
already exposed this limit. A nested ARM warm start now reproduced the same
zero/ffff calibration globals and corrupted exception vectors. Give q800 a
20 ms maximum. Keep the 100 us quiet release, cancellation on a new timer
load, explicit off switch, and hard upper bound. Other VIA classes and the
PowerPC lock are unchanged; no ROM code or global clock is modified.

diff --git a/hw/misc/mac_via.c b/hw/misc/mac_via.c
--- a/hw/misc/mac_via.c
+++ b/hw/misc/mac_via.c
@@ -1339,7 +1339,7 @@
     DEFINE_PROP_UINT32("x-t2-hold-quiet-us", MOS6522Q800VIA1State,
                        parent_obj.t2_hold_quiet_us, 100),
     DEFINE_PROP_UINT32("x-t2-hold-max-us", MOS6522Q800VIA1State,
-                       parent_obj.t2_hold_max_us, 4000),
+                       parent_obj.t2_hold_max_us, 20000),
     DEFINE_PROP_DRIVE("drive", MOS6522Q800VIA1State, blk),
